    <!-- How to Play Screen -->
    <string name="how_to_play_title">How to Play</string>
    <string name="how_to_play_subtitle">Fast-paced timed chess with no check</string>
    <string name="how_to_play_skip">Skip</string>
    <string name="how_to_play_got_it">Got it</string>
    <string name="how_to_play_before">1. Before</string>
    <string name="how_to_play_after">2. After</string>
    <string name="how_to_play_points_value_format">%1$d pts</string>
    <string name="how_to_play_points_value_single_format">%1$d pt</string>
    <string name="how_to_play_clock_active_sample" translatable="false">01:24</string>
    <string name="how_to_play_clock_paused_sample" translatable="false">01:45</string>

    <string name="how_to_play_sec1_title">1. Goal of the Game</string>
    <string name="how_to_play_sec1_body">Have more points on the board when the clock reaches 0. Protect high-value pieces and capture enemy material to take the lead.</string>

    <string name="how_to_play_sec2_title">2. Board &amp; Starting Setup</string>
    <string name="how_to_play_sec2_body">Played on a standard 8×8 board with all 16 pieces per side. White always moves first from the bottom ranks.</string>

    <string name="how_to_play_sec3_title">3. Pawn</string>
    <string name="how_to_play_sec3_body">Moves 1 square forward (or 2 on its first move), and captures 1 square diagonally forward. Never captures straight ahead.</string>

    <string name="how_to_play_sec4_title">4. Knight</string>
    <string name="how_to_play_sec4_body">Moves in an L-shape (2 squares one way, then 1 to the side). It is the only piece that can jump over other pieces.</string>

    <string name="how_to_play_sec5_title">5. Bishop</string>
    <string name="how_to_play_sec5_body">Slides diagonally any number of unobstructed squares. Each bishop stays on squares of its starting color.</string>

    <string name="how_to_play_sec6_title">6. Rook</string>
    <string name="how_to_play_sec6_body">Slides horizontally or vertically any number of unobstructed squares along ranks and files.</string>

    <string name="how_to_play_sec7_title">7. Queen</string>
    <string name="how_to_play_sec7_body">Combines the power of Rook and Bishop: slides any unobstructed distance in a straight line or diagonally.</string>

    <string name="how_to_play_sec8_title">8. King</string>
    <string name="how_to_play_sec8_body">Moves 1 square in any direction (horizontal, vertical, or diagonal). Worth 7 points — the most valuable piece on the board.</string>

    <string name="how_to_play_sec9_title">9. Capturing</string>
    <string name="how_to_play_sec9_body">Land on an enemy piece\'s square to remove it from the board and reduce your opponent\'s total board points.</string>

    <string name="how_to_play_sec10_title">10. Castling</string>
    <string name="how_to_play_sec10_body">King moves 2 squares toward an unmoved Rook, and the Rook jumps over. Allowed even through attacked squares if the path is clear!</string>

    <string name="how_to_play_sec11_title">11. En Passant</string>
    <string name="how_to_play_sec11_body">If an enemy pawn advances 2 squares beside your pawn, you may capture it diagonally on the very next turn as if it moved 1 square.</string>

    <string name="how_to_play_sec12_title">12. Pawn Promotion</string>
    <string name="how_to_play_sec12_body">When a pawn reaches the last row, immediately promote it to a Queen, Rook, Bishop, or Knight to boost your board points.</string>

    <string name="how_to_play_sec13_title">13. No Check, No Checkmate</string>
    <string name="how_to_play_sec13_body">There is no check or checkmate! Kings can move onto attacked squares and be captured like any other piece — the game keeps going.</string>

    <string name="how_to_play_sec14_title">14. Points Table</string>
    <string name="how_to_play_sec14_body">Every piece left on the board counts toward your score: Pawn 1, Knight 2, Bishop 3, Rook 4, Queen 5, King 7.</string>

    <string name="how_to_play_sec15_title">15. Timer</string>
    <string name="how_to_play_sec15_body">Each side gets 1 or 2 minutes total with no increment. Your clock runs only during your own turn.</string>

    <string name="how_to_play_sec16_title">16. How to Win</string>
    <string name="how_to_play_sec16_body">When either clock hits 0, the game ends immediately. The side with more points on the board wins; equal points is a draw.</string>

    <string name="how_to_play_sec17_title">17. No Legal Moves</string>
    <string name="how_to_play_sec17_body">If a player has no legal moves on their turn, their turn is skipped while their clock continues running until time runs out.</string>

    <string name="how_to_play_sec18_title">18. Winning Probability Bar</string>
    <string name="how_to_play_sec18_body">Raw point totals stay hidden during play. Read the live orange-vs-dark bar to see who is ahead in material and remaining time.</string>

